# Parity fixture (TAGGED / cell half) for the Phase 2 bridge's
# ``-tagged_terms`` experiment -- Task 3 parity corpus.
#
# Identical to struct_tabling.clausal (recursion + compound answers, the
# fixture Task 4's interning measurement depends on) apart from the added
# directive and the module name.  cons/2 is a declared data functor with no
# clauses, so every ``cons(N, T)`` construction/match in a flagged module
# lowers to the cell literal ``('cons', n, t)`` instead of a class instance;
# the atom ``nil`` stays a class atom either way (Phase 3 does the atom
# pivot, not this bridge).
#
# Self-contained: every functor it constructs or matches is declared here.
-module(struct_tabling_tagged, [
    cons(H, T),
    nil,
    Nats(N, L),
])
-table(Nats/2)

Nats(0, nil),
Nats(N, cons(N, T)) <- (
    N > 0,
    N1 == N - 1,
    Nats(N1, T)
)
